{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SchurPrincipalBranching","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SchurPrincipalBranching","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.QRatioBetaFactors","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.PairProductSplit","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.VandermondeUpdateRatio"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.not_isAddableCell_rowEnd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.not_isAddableCell_rowEnd","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L240-L247","doc":"The contrapositive, in the form `qratio_prod_eq_zero_of_not_addable` consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.isAddableCell_rowEnd_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.isAddableCell_rowEnd_iff","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L218-L238","doc":"**Row `a` takes a box exactly when `a = 0` or the row above is strictly longer.**\n\nThe other two clauses of `IsAddableCell` are automatic at the end of a row: `(a, μ_a)` is never in\n`μ`, and its left neighbour is present whenever the row is nonempty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qratio_prod_eq_zero_of_not_addable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qratio_prod_eq_zero_of_not_addable","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L194-L214","doc":"**A row that cannot take a box contributes nothing.**\n\nRow `a > 0` is addable exactly when `μ_{a−1} > μ_a`.  When instead `μ_{a−1} = μ_a`, the β-numbers\nsatisfy `β_{a−1} = β_a + 1`, so `Q·x_a = x_{a−1}` and the `j = a−1` factor of the `q`-ratio's\nnumerator is zero.\n\nThis is what lets a sum over **all `r` rows** stand in for a sum over the **addable** ones — the\n`schurPrincipal`-level counterpart of `QOU.Mathlib.vandPairProd_update_eq_zero`, and the reason the\n`r = 2` chain's `rowLen_two_addCell_row2` needs no general-`r` analogue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.schurPrincipal_addCell_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.schurPrincipal_addCell_eq","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L161-L192","doc":"**The box-addition ratio, in quotient form — the branching hypothesis itself.**\n\n`s_{μ+□ at row a}(1,…,Q^{r−1}) = (∏_{j ≠ a} (Q·x_a − x_j)/(x_a − x_j)) · s_μ(1,…,Q^{r−1})`,\n`x_i = Q^{β_i}`.\n\nThis is `hw` of `QOU.Mathlib.sum_eq_bracket_mul_of_qratio_scaling` for `schurPrincipal`, so with it\n`∑_a s_{μ+□ at a} = [r]_Q · s_μ` — general-`r` branching for the corpus weight.\n\nThe two extra hypotheses over the cross-multiplied form are the price of dividing: `levelConst` and\nthe row-column product must be invertible.  Both are products of `1 − Q^k` at nonzero `k` (the\nβ-numbers are distinct by `betaR_lt`), so both hold under the same root-of-unity genericity that\n`schurPrincipal_eq_zero_iff` already assumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qratio_prod_eq_rowColProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qratio_prod_eq_rowColProd","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L122-L159","doc":"**The `q`-ratio is `Q^a` times the row-column ratio.**\n\n`∏_{j ≠ a} (Q·x_a − x_j)/(x_a − x_j) = Q^a · (row·col)_ν / (row·col)_μ`,  `x_i = Q^{β_i}`.\n\nUnconditional beyond `Q ≠ 0`: a product of quotients is the quotient of the products in any field,\nand the two `QRatioBetaFactors` lemmas supply the factorwise identity — `j > a` exactly, `j < a`\nwith one `Q`.  The `a` copies of `Q` from the rows above are what becomes `Q^a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.schurPrincipal_addCell_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.schurPrincipal_addCell_mul","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L87-L118","doc":"**The box-addition ratio for `schurPrincipal`, cross-multiplied.**\n\n`s_ν · C · (row·col)_μ = Q^{a} · (row·col)_ν · s_μ · C`,   `ν = μ + □ at row `a`.\n\nDividing (where the factors are invertible) gives\n`s_ν/s_μ = Q^a · (row·col)_ν/(row·col)_μ`, and `QRatioBetaFactors` identifies that right-hand side\nwith `∏_{j ≠ a}(Q·x_a − x_j)/(x_a − x_j)` at `x_i = Q^{β_i}` — the hypothesis\n`QOU.Mathlib.sum_eq_bracket_mul_of_qratio_scaling` is waiting on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.betaPairProd_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.betaPairProd_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L74-L85","doc":"**Only the pairs involving `a` change.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.schurPrincipal_mul_levelConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.schurPrincipal_mul_levelConst","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L65-L72","doc":"The closed form, in interval indexing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.rowColProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.rowColProd","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L60-L63","doc":"The row-`a` and column-`a` factors of `P_μ` — the ones a box at row `a` changes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.levelConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.levelConst","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L56-L58","doc":"`C(r)`, the `μ`-independent constant of the closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.betaPairProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.betaPairProd","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L52-L54","doc":"`P_μ = ∏_{i<j<r} (1 − Q^{β_i − β_j})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.prod_offset_eq_prod_Ico","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.prod_offset_eq_prod_Ico","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SchurPrincipalBranching.lean#L44-L48","doc":"Offset indexing (`∏_{k < r−(i+1)}`) and interval indexing (`∏_{j ∈ Ico (i+1) r}`) agree. ","signatureChunk":0}]}